# QDQC · Tech Stack

## Canonical stack

| Layer | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| App | Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript |
| UI | React + Tailwind CSS |
| 3D | Three.js + React Three Fiber + Drei + postprocessing |
| Motion | **GSAP + ScrollTrigger only** (no Framer Motion / Anime / Locomotive) |
| Scroll | Lenis, synced with GSAP ticker |
| State | Zustand |
| Audio | Howler.js behind `MusicEngine` |

## Architecture

- **One persistent WebGL Canvas** (`position: fixed`) for the whole story world. Never spawn a new WebGL context per chapter.
- DOM story layer scrolls above the canvas; camera / lighting / objects scrub on the same `storyProgress`.
- Build a thin **Story Engine**: chapter progress → camera + objects + text + music + particles.
- Chapter data is declarative (`data/chapters.ts`); pages consume, not hardcode timelines.

## Animation policy

- Slow > many. Prefer scrubbed timelines over flashy loops.
- Allow: butterfly flight, water, moon breath, bridge lamps, petal drift, night→dawn color.
- Forbid: heart explosions, spinning headlines, unchecked 3D flex.

## Performance from day one

- Image: AVIF/WebP derivatives in `web/public` (sources untouched).
- Load: Hero → current chapter → preload next.
- Cap particles / bloom / DPR on mobile & low-power; respect reduced motion.
